---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "About";
const description = "About your blog.";
const permalink = `${Astro.site?.href}about`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  permalink={permalink}
  current="about"
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Kathy Shumway</h1>

    <figure class="about-image">
      <dv class="img-container">
        <img src="/assets/Kathy_Photo_Smile.jpg" alt="Photo of Kathy Shumway" />
      </dv>
      <figcaption>
        <a href="https://alexhealyphoto.com/" target="_blank"
          >Photo by Alex Healy</a
        >
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <p>
      Kathy is a top-producing real estate agent in Ulster County, proudly
      serving buyers and sellers throughout the Hudson Valley for over 20 years.
      With more than 100 successful sales and a consistent 5-star rating on
      Zillow, she’s known for her local expertise, integrity, and strong
      negotiation skills that deliver results.
    </p>

    <p>
      She first arrived in Woodstock, New York, in the summer of 1994, chasing
      adventure in her early twenties. The area’s creative energy and natural
      beauty immediately drew her in. After a period of traveling between
      Toronto and the Catskills, she decided to settle in Willow, where she
      raised her two children and built a life surrounded by community and
      nature.
    </p>

    <p>
      When Kathy sold her first home—with the help of a local agent friend—it
      quickly went to the founders of the Woodstock Animal Sanctuary. The
      experience inspired her to pursue a career in real estate, combining her
      love for homes, people, and the Hudson Valley lifestyle.
    </p>

    <p>
      Today, she continues her work with House of Kathy, bringing energy,
      insight, and dedication to every transaction. Whether guiding first-time
      buyers, seasoned investors, or long-time residents, Kathy takes pride in
      being a steady advocate and an experienced negotiator.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Hudson Valley offers something for everyone—from grand estates to cozy
      seasonal cottages. Its breathtaking landscapes, artistic spirit, and
      vibrant four seasons make it one of New York’s most desirable places to
      live. Winter weekends invite skiing at Windham, Hunter, or Belleayre;
      summer brings endless hiking, festivals, and outdoor adventures; and
      autumn paints the mountains in unforgettable color.
    </p>

    <p>
      Local life is rich with character—farmers markets, wineries, and small
      businesses give Ulster County its unique charm. It’s this combination of
      nature, creativity, and community that makes living here so rewarding—and
      why Kathy is passionate about helping others experience it for themselves.
    </p>

    <p>
      As a certified EcoBroker, Kathy also specializes in sustainable and
      environmentally conscious homes. She even built her own eco-friendly
      residence using organic paints, stains, and bamboo flooring. Whether
      you’re buying your dream home or selling your property, Kathy is ready to
      guide you every step of the way.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .container {
      max-width: 95%;
      text-align: left;
    }
    .about-image {
      height: 400px;
      float: right;
      margin: 0 0 2em 2em;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .image-container {
      border-radius: 100%;
      overflow: hidden;
      height: 200px;
      width: 200px;
    }

    .about-image img {
      width: 250px;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center;
      padding: 2px;
    }

    .about-image figcaption {
      margin-top: 0.6em;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
      font-style: italic;
    }

    .about-image figcaption a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1020px) {
      h1 {
        text-align: center;
      }

      .about-image {
        float: none;
        margin: 1.5em auto 2em;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
